EXPERIMENT-6: Leader Election — Bully and Ring Algorithms
==========================================================

REQUIREMENT:
- Java JDK must be installed
- Check: java -version


*** BULLY ALGORITHM ***
-----------------------

1. Compile:
   javac BullyAlgorithm.java

2. Run:
   java BullyAlgorithm

How to use:
- Enter the number of processes (e.g. 4)
  >> Processes are automatically numbered 1, 2, 3, 4 ...
- Enter a process number to crash (e.g. 3)
  >> This simulates that process 3 has failed
- Enter the process number that starts the election (e.g. 1)
  >> Must be a number that is NOT crashed
  >> The program will show election messages and announce the leader

Common mistake: Entering the crashed process as the initiator
>> The crashed process cannot start the election. Enter a different process.


*** RING ALGORITHM ***
----------------------

1. Compile:
   javac RingAlgorithm.java

2. Run:
   java RingAlgorithm

How to use:
- Enter the number of processes (e.g. 4)
- Enter a process number to crash (e.g. 2)
- Enter the initiator process number (e.g. 1)
  >> The election message will travel around the ring
  >> Active processes add their ID to the message
  >> The process with the highest ID becomes the leader

Common mistake: Entering a process number larger than total processes
>> If you enter 4 processes, valid numbers are 1 to 4 only.


ERROR (both programs):
- 'javac' is not recognized? >> Install JDK and add to PATH.
- ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException? >> You entered a process number outside the valid range.